{"name":"Milestone","hex":"#7f848a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"milestone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stone milepost (or by extension in other materials), one of a series of numbered markers placed along a road at regular intervals, typically at the side of the road or in a median.","An important event in a person's life or career, in the history of a nation, in the life of some project, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place milestones along (a road, etc.).","To plan out a project as a series of major steps."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milestone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Milestone","blocks":[{"text":"A milestone is a numbered marker placed on a route such as a road, railway line, canal or boundary. They can indicate the distance to towns, cities, and other places or landmarks like mileage signs; or they can give their position on the route relative to some datum location. On roads they are typically located at the side or in a median or central reservation. They are alternatively known as mile markers, mileposts or mile posts. A \"kilometric point\" is a term used in metricated areas, where distances are commonly measured in kilometres instead of miles. \"Distance marker\" is a generic unit-agnostic term."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Cumberland_258.jpg/330px-Cumberland_258.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milestone","wikidata":"Q10145"},{"title":"Milestone (Italian company)","blocks":[{"text":"Milestone S.r.l. is an Italian video game developer based in Milan. Founded in 1994 by Antonio Farina, the studio specialises in racing games, especially motorcycle racing games. The company began under the name Graffiti, developing the car racing game Screamer. After the studio rebranded as Milestone in 1996, it used Screamer's success for multi-game publishing deals with Virgin Interactive and Electronic Arts. The poor performance of Racing Evoluzione, published by Atari with little marketing, lead to key figures leaving Milestone. As part of Leader Group from 2002 on, the studio hired many younger developers and developed multiple games for multiple platforms, including several based on the Superbike World Championship. This shaped Milestone's identity as a developer of motorcycle racing games. After detaching from Leader Group in 2011, the studio obtained the license for MotoGP games in 2013. In 2019, Milestone was acquired by Koch Media."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Milestone_%28Italian_company%29.svg/330px-Milestone_%28Italian_company%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milestone_(Italian_company)","wikidata":"Q1134915"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Milestone%40Penrhosgarnedd_2.jpg/500px-Milestone%40Penrhosgarnedd_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Milestone%40Penrhosgarnedd_2.jpg/500px-Milestone%40Penrhosgarnedd_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Slate milestone near Bangor, Wales","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilestone%40Penrhosgarnedd_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Geira_Milha_XXIX_caminho.jpg/500px-Geira_Milha_XXIX_caminho.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Geira_Milha_XXIX_caminho.jpg/1280px-Geira_Milha_XXIX_caminho.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Geira_Milha_XXIX_caminho.jpg/500px-Geira_Milha_XXIX_caminho.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam